  "master": {
    "html": "<div class=\"run-head\">GEOZINE · ISSUE 1</div>\n<div class=\"folio\">— {page} of {pages} —</div>",
    "css": ".run-head {\n  position: absolute;\n  top: 6px;\n  left: 20px;\n  right: 20px;\n  font-size: 8px;\n  letter-spacing: 2px;\n  border-bottom: 1px solid #000;\n  padding-bottom: 1px;\n}\n.folio {\n  position: absolute;\n  bottom: 6px;\n  left: 0;\n  right: 0;\n  text-align: center;\n  font-size: 9px;\n}"
  },
  "story": {
    "html": "<h3 class=\"f-pixel\">The 64K Print Shop</h3>\n<p>In 1986 Berkeley Softworks shipped GeoPublish for GEOS, the graphical desktop that made a Commodore 64 behave like a tiny Macintosh. In 64 kilobytes of memory it let anyone with a dot-matrix printer lay out a newsletter with columns, headlines and pictures.</p>\n<p>You did not type onto the page. You drew boxes on it, then poured a geoWrite document into the first box. Whatever did not fit spilled into the next linked box, even on another page.</p>\n<blockquote class=\"pull\">“Draw the boxes first. Pour the words in after.”</blockquote>\n<p>That is what you are reading now. This article lives in one place, the Story, and is poured into every page with “Flow story onto this page” ticked. Edit a sentence and everything after it reflows.</p>\n<p>GeoPublish had a mode for each job:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><b>Master Page</b>: the running head and page number on every page.</li>\n<li><b>Page Layout</b>: text regions and columns.</li>\n<li><b>Page Graphics</b>: lines, boxes and 8×8 fill patterns.</li>\n<li><b>Preview</b>: the whole page shrunk down before printing.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>This editor borrows all of it. On page three the story runs through two columns by itself. A paragraph that is too long is split between two words and continues on the next page with no indent, like a newspaper.</p>\n<p>The rest of this issue is a tour: the tool box on page five, photo scraps on six, folding on seven.</p>",
    "css": "p {\n  text-indent: 1.2em;\n  margin-bottom: 4px;\n  line-height: 1.35;\n}\np.zcont {\n  text-indent: 0;\n}\nh3 {\n  font-size: 11px;\n  margin-bottom: 4px;\n}\nol {\n  margin: 2px 0 6px 20px;\n  line-height: 1.3;\n}\nli {\n  margin-bottom: 2px;\n}"
  },
  "settings": {
    "cutMarks": true
  },
